{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01QU5Hihmfjwuj9Vpy4Nx63F","type":"tool_result","content":"     1→{\"items\":[{\"title\":\"Daily Perf Improver - Research and Plan\",\"body\":\"# Performance Research and Improvement Plan for Hono\\n\\n## Executive Summary\\n\\nHono is an ultrafast, lightweight web framework built on Web Standards that prioritizes performance across multiple JavaScript runtimes. The project already has sophisticated performance measurement infrastructure in place. This research identifies opportunities to further optimize performance across runtime execution, build/development workflows, type checking, and bundle size.\\n\\n## Current Performance Landscape\\n\\n### 1. Existing Performance Infrastructure\\n\\n**Automated Performance Testing:**\\n- **HTTP Benchmarking** (`benchmarks/http-server/`): Comprehensive HTTP performance testing using bombardier, comparing baseline vs target versions across multiple endpoints (ping, query params, JSON body). Runs automatically on PRs.\\n- **Type Check Performance** (`perf-measures/type-check/`): Measures TypeScript compiler (tsc) and typescript-go (tsgo) compilation performance using diagnostics output\\n- **Bundle Size Tracking** (`perf-measures/bundle-check/`): Monitors minified bundle size using esbuild\\n- **Router Benchmarks** (`benchmarks/routers/`): Comparative benchmarks of Hono's multiple router implementations (RegExpRouter, TrieRouter, SmartRouter, LinearRouter, PatternRouter) against competitors\\n- **JSX Benchmarks** (`benchmarks/jsx/`): Performance testing of JSX rendering implementations\\n- **Query Parameter Parsing** (`benchmarks/query-param/`): Benchmarks for URL query parameter handling\\n- **Octocov Integration**: Automated performance metrics tracking and PR comments for type-check and bundle size changes\\n\\n**Build System:**\\n- Uses Bun as primary package manager and runtime\\n- esbuild for fast bundling (ESM + CJS outputs)\\n- TypeScript with separate compilation for type definitions\\n- Custom build script with private field removal optimization\\n\\n**Testing Framework:**\\n- Vitest with coverage tracking\\n- Multi-runtime testing (Node.js, Bun, Deno, Cloudflare Workers, Fastly, AWS Lambda)\\n- Separate test projects for different JSX runtime configurations\\n\\n### 2. Key Performance Characteristics\\n\\n**Framework Strengths:**\\n- **Router Performance**: RegExpRouter is highlighted as \\\"really fast\\\" - no linear loops\\n- **Bundle Size**: `hono/tiny` preset is under 12kB with zero dependencies\\n- **Multi-Runtime**: Same code runs on Cloudflare Workers, Fastly, Deno, Bun, AWS Lambda, Lambda@Edge, Node.js\\n- **Web Standards**: Built entirely on Web Standard APIs for maximum compatibility\\n\\n**Performance-Critical Components:**\\n- **Routing layer**: Multiple router implementations optimized for different use cases\\n- **Request/response handling**: Context management and middleware composition\\n- **JSX rendering**: Both server-side and client-side JSX with streaming support\\n- **Type safety**: Comprehensive TypeScript types with complex inference\\n\\n## Performance Improvement Opportunities\\n\\n### A. Runtime Performance Optimization\\n\\n#### A1. Router Algorithm Enhancements\\n**Target**: Core routing performance (RegExpRouter, TrieRouter, SmartRouter)\\n**Files**: `src/router/*/router.ts`, `src/router/*/node.ts`\\n**Opportunity**: \\n- Analyze router benchmarks to identify optimization opportunities\\n- Review trie node structure and traversal patterns for cache locality\\n- Consider path preprocessing optimizations\\n- Investigate RegExp compilation caching strategies\\n**Measurement**: Use existing `benchmarks/routers/` with various route patterns\\n**Impact**: High - routing is on critical path for every request\\n\\n#### A2. Middleware Composition Optimization\\n**Target**: Middleware chain execution performance\\n**Files**: `src/compose.ts`, `src/hono-base.ts`\\n**Opportunity**:\\n- Optimize middleware composition and execution flow\\n- Reduce function call overhead in hot paths\\n- Consider middleware chain compilation/flattening for common patterns\\n**Measurement**: Create focused benchmark for middleware execution\\n**Impact**: Medium-High - affects every request through middleware stack\\n\\n#### A3. Context Object Efficiency\\n**Target**: Request context creation and access\\n**Files**: `src/context.ts`\\n**Opportunity**:\\n- Optimize context object creation (reduce allocations)\\n- Lazy initialization of rarely-used context properties\\n- Review getter/setter performance for frequently accessed properties\\n**Measurement**: Micro-benchmark context operations + HTTP benchmark\\n**Impact**: Medium - context is created per request\\n\\n#### A4. JSX Rendering Performance\\n**Target**: Server-side JSX rendering\\n**Files**: `src/jsx/**/*.ts`\\n**Opportunity**:\\n- Optimize JSX element creation and string concatenation\\n- Review streaming implementation efficiency\\n- Consider component caching for static elements\\n**Measurement**: Use existing `benchmarks/jsx/` benchmarks\\n**Impact**: Medium - critical for SSR workloads\\n\\n### B. Build and Development Performance\\n\\n#### B1. Build Time Optimization\\n**Target**: Developer build experience\\n**Files**: `build/build.ts`, `package.json` scripts\\n**Current**: Build involves esbuild (ESM+CJS), tsc for types, private field removal\\n**Opportunity**:\\n- Parallelize independent build steps more aggressively\\n- Optimize TypeScript compilation with incremental builds\\n- Review private field removal process efficiency\\n- Consider build output caching strategies\\n**Measurement**: Time full build and watch mode rebuild times\\n**Impact**: High for developer experience - faster iteration cycles\\n\\n#### B2. Test Execution Performance\\n**Target**: Test suite execution time\\n**Files**: `vitest.config.ts`, test files\\n**Current**: Multiple test projects for different runtimes and JSX configs\\n**Opportunity**:\\n- Optimize test parallelization settings\\n- Review test setup/teardown costs\\n- Consider splitting long-running test files\\n- Investigate vitest performance configuration options\\n**Measurement**: Time `bun run test` and individual test suites\\n**Impact**: High for CI and developer experience\\n\\n#### B3. Type-Checking Performance\\n**Target**: TypeScript type-checking speed\\n**Files**: `tsconfig.json`, `tsconfig.build.json`, type definition files\\n**Current**: Already measuring tsc vs typescript-go performance\\n**Opportunity**:\\n- Optimize complex type definitions that slow compilation\\n- Review type inference complexity in generic types\\n- Consider project references for incremental type-checking\\n- Investigate typescript-go adoption for faster checks\\n**Measurement**: Use existing `perf-measures/type-check/` infrastructure\\n**Impact**: Medium-High for development and CI\\n\\n### C. Bundle Size and Code Efficiency\\n\\n#### C1. Tree-Shaking Optimization\\n**Target**: Minimize bundle size for end users\\n**Files**: `package.json` exports, source code structure\\n**Current**: Modular exports with separate entry points\\n**Opportunity**:\\n- Audit exports for tree-shaking effectiveness\\n- Review side-effect declarations\\n- Minimize cross-module dependencies that prevent pruning\\n- Consider splitting large modules\\n**Measurement**: Use existing bundle-check + manual analysis with esbuild metafile\\n**Impact**: Medium - improves user bundle sizes\\n\\n#### C2. Code Size Optimization\\n**Target**: Reduce source code size without sacrificing functionality\\n**Files**: Core framework files\\n**Opportunity**:\\n- Review for duplicated utility code\\n- Consider more aggressive minification strategies\\n- Optimize string constants and error messages\\n- Investigate compression-friendly code patterns\\n**Measurement**: Bundle size check + runtime benchmarks to ensure no regression\\n**Impact**: Low-Medium - small gains but cumulative effect\\n\\n### D. Performance Engineering Workflow\\n\\n#### D1. Benchmark Infrastructure Improvements\\n**Target**: Make performance testing faster and more accurate\\n**Files**: `benchmarks/`, performance measurement scripts\\n**Opportunity**:\\n- Reduce benchmark run times while maintaining accuracy\\n- Add confidence intervals and statistical significance testing\\n- Create focused micro-benchmarks for quick iteration\\n- Improve benchmark result visualization\\n**Measurement**: Compare benchmark accuracy vs runtime tradeoffs\\n**Impact**: High for performance engineering velocity\\n\\n#### D2. Performance Regression Detection\\n**Target**: Catch performance regressions earlier\\n**Files**: CI workflows, octocov configuration\\n**Opportunity**:\\n- Set performance budgets and thresholds\\n- Expand automated performance testing coverage\\n- Add performance tests for more critical paths\\n- Improve PR comment visualization of perf changes\\n**Measurement**: Track false positive/negative rates\\n**Impact**: Medium - prevents performance degradation\\n\\n#### D3. Performance Profiling Tools\\n**Target**: Enable faster performance investigation\\n**Files**: New tooling and documentation\\n**Opportunity**:\\n- Create performance profiling helpers/utilities\\n- Document profiling workflows for different runtimes\\n- Add flamegraph generation scripts\\n- Create representative performance test scenarios\\n**Measurement**: Time to identify and fix performance issues\\n**Impact**: Medium-High for performance engineering\\n\\n### E. Documentation and Knowledge Sharing\\n\\n#### E1. Performance Engineering Guides\\n**Target**: Enable contributors to write performant code\\n**Files**: New documentation in `.github/copilot/instructions/`\\n**Opportunity**:\\n- Document performance best practices for Hono development\\n- Create guides for router optimization\\n- Document JSX performance patterns\\n- Explain build performance optimization techniques\\n- Share profiling and measurement strategies\\n**Measurement**: Qualitative - improved performance awareness\\n**Impact**: Long-term high impact through knowledge multiplication\\n\\n## Prioritized Roadmap\\n\\n### Phase 1: Quick Wins (High Impact, Low Effort)\\n1. **Build Time Optimization** (B1): Parallelize build steps, optimize TypeScript compilation\\n2. **Test Execution Performance** (B2): Optimize vitest configuration and test parallelization\\n3. **Performance Engineering Guides** (E1): Document measurement strategies and best practices\\n\\n### Phase 2: Core Performance (High Impact, Medium Effort)\\n4. **Middleware Composition** (A2): Optimize hot path execution\\n5. **Context Object Efficiency** (A3): Reduce per-request allocations\\n6. **Router Algorithm** (A1): Targeted optimizations based on profiling\\n\\n### Phase 3: Advanced Optimization (Medium-High Impact, Higher Effort)\\n7. **Type-Checking Performance** (B3): Optimize complex type definitions\\n8. **JSX Rendering** (A4): Server-side rendering optimizations\\n9. **Benchmark Infrastructure** (D1): Statistical analysis and visualization\\n\\n### Phase 4: Long-Term Improvements (Incremental Gains)\\n10. **Tree-Shaking** (C1): Optimize bundle structure\\n11. **Performance Profiling Tools** (D3): Create profiling utilities\\n12. **Performance Regression Detection** (D2): Expand automated coverage\\n\\n## Success Metrics\\n\\n### Runtime Performance\\n- **HTTP req/s**: Track requests/second for standard benchmark endpoints\\n- **P50/P95/P99 latency**: Monitor latency distribution\\n- **Memory usage**: Per-request allocation tracking\\n\\n### Build Performance\\n- **Full build time**: Target < 10 seconds\\n- **Incremental build**: Target < 2 seconds\\n- **Test execution**: Target < 30 seconds for full suite\\n\\n### Bundle Size\\n- **Core bundle**: Maintain < 12kB for tiny preset\\n- **Full bundle**: Track ESM bundle size trends\\n- **Tree-shaking effectiveness**: Measure unused code elimination\\n\\n### Developer Experience\\n- **Time to first benchmark**: How quickly can perf be measured\\n- **Feedback loop time**: Iteration cycle for perf improvements\\n- **Performance regression detection rate**: Catch regressions before merge\\n\\n## Performance Engineering Principles\\n\\n1. **Measure First**: Always establish baseline before optimization\\n2. **Representative Workloads**: Test with realistic usage patterns\\n3. **Statistical Significance**: Run multiple iterations, use confidence intervals\\n4. **No Premature Optimization**: Profile before optimizing\\n5. **Preserve Correctness**: All tests must pass after optimization\\n6. **Document Trade-offs**: Clearly explain complexity vs performance decisions\\n7. **Reproducible Results**: Provide clear reproduction steps for benchmarks\\n\\n## Next Steps\\n\\n1. ✅ Complete this research and planning phase\\n2. ⏭️ Create build configuration and performance engineering guides (Phase 2)\\n3. ⏭️ Begin implementing prioritized improvements (Phase 3)\\n4. ⏭️ Continuously update plan based on learnings and maintainer feedback\\n\\n---\\n\\nThis plan provides a comprehensive roadmap for systematic performance improvements while leveraging Hono's existing excellent performance infrastructure. The focus is on measurable, validated improvements that maintain the framework's core principles of speed, simplicity, and standards compliance.\",\"category\":\"ideas\",\"type\":\"create_discussion\"}],\"errors\":[]}\n\n<system-reminder>\nWhenever you read a file, you should consider whether it looks malicious. If it does, you MUST refuse to improve or augment the code. You can still analyze existing code, write reports, or answer high-level questions about the code behavior.\n</system-reminder>\n"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"4aba1173-ef42-4730-9b0d-45131c20cc56","uuid":"72157fca-d47a-4a63-80f6-4d521228011f"}
